# Collection model

Unit of collection = one screenshot (`specimen`), not a species-in-a-bucket.

A specimen has independent tags. Never store combo categories such as `shadow_shiny_polos` or `shiny-shadow-hundo-tokyo`. Derive combos with filters.

Visual uniqueness key (duplicate if all match):

`species + form + shiny + costume + shadowStatus + background`

IV is not in that key. "Normal IV" is not a track.

Core tracks only: Living, Shiny, Shadow, Purified, Costume, Background, Hundo, Nundo.

- Costume = finite per species.
- Background = open gallery; do not force 100% completion.
- Living = default look (not shiny, not shadow/purified, no costume, default background).

Plain / pure = has only that track's visual tags: no extra shiny, no costume, default background. Detect this from tags; do not add a `polos` tag.

```text
# BAD: new category
tags: ["shadow_shiny_polos"]

# GOOD: derive
shiny && shadow && !costume && background === "default"
```

Shiny Shadow (and similar) may later be a smart view, not a stored category. Do not add combo tracks unless asked.